description:
FILED s534a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-08) as the lever the evaluation recommends (docs/method-lookup-eval-s534.md §4-§6; awaiting the USER's word).  Prototypes in the s534a worktree: scratch/s534a/rt/proto-b.lisp (hits), proto-e.lisp (+ misses), proto-f.lisp (+ the cached ancestry) with their .diff files.

THE DESIGN (from proto-e): the s473s own-class table `*pcl-own-method-cache*` gains INHERITED entries (class as the invocant spells it, method name) -> a %pcl-mentry: the resolved SYMBOL (or :MISS) and one LINK per class the DFS passed before the answer -- that class's interned `@isa` symbol, a COPY of the parent names it read there, and its interned `pl-NAME` symbol.  A hit re-reads every link: the current @ISA contents equal the copy name by name, the `pl-NAME` symbol still has no live sub (a method defined later in a closer class wins), the stash-deleted mark is off, and the found symbol is live.  A miss entry also carries UNIVERSAL's chain and answers through `%pcl-after-chain-miss` (isa / DOES / can / import / AUTOLOAD / die, the same cond in the same order).  Nothing is invalidated and NO array writer changes -- which is why this needs none of #582's original @ISA-write audit (217 runtime definitions write vectors; option (c) measured, rejected).  Inputs NOT re-read, each with its single writer: a name's package (`p-stash-assign` -> clrhash), a (package, name) -> symbol pair (`p-import-perl-symbol`'s `shadowing-import` arm uninterns a local symbol -> add a clrhash there; LATENT for the shipped own-class entries too).

MEASURED (BENCH_RT_B A/B vs base 95a1de03, best of 5, the doc's §4 table): proto-f (hits + misses + the cached ancestry) methinh -65.1 % (3.87x -> 1.35x of perl), methinh3 -77.3 % (7.38x -> 1.68x), methpoly -63.6 % (3.45x -> 1.26x), ovlbool -67.2 % (6.34x -> 2.08x, the overload half #4524), methret / ovlsub / json-rt / moo-objs inside the control band, the PPI parse -37.3 % (4.38x -> 2.75x).  proto-b (hits only) gave PPI only -6.6 %: PPI's hot inherited call is the `->isa` MISS through Params::Util::_INSTANCE, and `->isa`'s answer rebuilt the ancestry list each call -- hence the miss entries (e: PPI -24.1 %) and the cached ancestry (f).  Build together with #4525 (the %p-isa-symbol guard).

THE BUILD (one runtime-only session; no emission change, no generation):
  1. port proto-f (= proto-e's hits and misses + the cached ancestry; the doc recommends it) into cl/pcl-runtime.lisp; the snapshot strings are COPIED with copy-seq (the prototype's %pcl-memo-key shares simple strings with @ISA -- no probe found an in-place element mutation, but the copy makes the content test independent of that);
  2. the clrhash in p-import-perl-symbol's shadowing-import arm;
  3. a CHECK MODE for one batch only -- `PCL_METHOD_CACHE_CHECK=1`: every cached hit or miss also runs the full walk and DIES naming class + method on a disagreement (rule 12) -- run over the gate, the sweep and the CPAN board, then deleted before the merge (the PCL_STMT_CHECK / PCL_BINDER_CHECK pattern);
  4. guards: a new `Pl/t/method-cache-02.t` carrying scratch/s534a/pr/matrix.pl's 61 cases (expected = perl's output, the 7 pre-existing divergences annotated as canaries with their tasks) + intern.pl's rows; an INVERSE mechanism row that fails on the base (after `$o->m` through three levels, `(pcl::%pcl-own-method-cached "D" "m")` answers a function); a TIMED row methinh3 <= 8 * perl + 0.5 s (relative, never absolute -- CI is ~3x slower).
BAR: the 4 inherited rows + methret ovlsub moo-objs json-rt A/B through `heavy.sh <label> bench` (+ a byte-identical control column); the PPI parse (scratch/s534a/bench-ppi.pl) BEFORE -> AFTER; gate + full sweep + the companion one-file legs mro/*.t, op/method.t, op/universal.t, lib/overload.t, uni/method.t; the CPAN board one-file runs of the PPI-using dists if any; EVERYDAY BEFORE -> AFTER.
